# The web unit tests in CI — one step, for the owner to apply
#
# WHY THIS IS A PATCH AND NOT A COMMIT: the GitHub App has NO
# workflows scope, so a change to .github/workflows/ci.yml cannot be
# pushed by the bot. This is the repo's established pattern — see
# docs/ci-workflow-patch-evidence.md and the 0056/0057 patch.
#
# WHAT IT ADDS: one step to the "Tests (vitest + postgis)" job, after
# the sourcing rating engine tests:
#
#   - name: Run the web unit tests
#     working-directory: apps/web
#     run: pnpm test
#
# WHAT IT FIXES: apps/web had no `test` script and no CI step, so the
# seven test files already in apps/web/src/lib/ — 125 assertions — were
# ORPHANED. They passed; nothing ran them. WP-A1 adds
# apps/web/src/lib/creditText.test.ts to that set, and this step is what
# makes it a gate instead of a comment.
#
# HOW TO APPLY (from the repository root):
#
#   git apply docs/ci-wp-a1-web-tests.patch
#
# The patch applies cleanly to ci.yml at this PR's base. It touches
# nothing else.
#
# WHAT TO EXPECT: the step runs 131 tests (125 existing + 6 new) with
# Node's built-in test runner. They need no database and no services.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index 482f2dd..747544f 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -1252,6 +1252,23 @@ jobs:
         working-directory: packages/sourcing
         run: pnpm test -- --reporter=verbose
 
+      # The web's unit tests (apps/web/src/lib/*.test.ts). These are
+      # PURE functions over plain data -- no database, no I/O -- and
+      # they use Node's built-in test runner, the same style as the
+      # seven files that were already there.
+      #
+      # WHY THIS STEP EXISTS: until now NOTHING ran them. The CI
+      # pipeline invoked `pnpm test` in apps/api and packages/sourcing
+      # only, and apps/web had no `test` script at all, so the seven
+      # existing web test files -- and the 125 assertions in them --
+      # were orphaned. They passed; nobody was checking.
+      #
+      # WP-A1 adds apps/web/src/lib/creditText.test.ts to that set, and
+      # this step is what makes it a gate rather than a comment.
+      - name: Run the web unit tests
+        working-directory: apps/web
+        run: pnpm test
+
   # ─── Job 2b: Accessibility gate (axe-core) ─────────────────────────
   #
   # WHY THIS JOB EXISTS
